1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,833
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,667
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:38,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:40,233 --> 00:00:42,100
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,433
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:54,600
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:55,700
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:57,200
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:00,533 --> 00:01:02,467
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:04,967 --> 00:01:07,833
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:12,600
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,233
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:15,233 --> 00:01:16,833
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:16,833 --> 00:01:21,100
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:23,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:25,367 --> 00:01:27,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:30,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:31,167
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:31,167 --> 00:01:32,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:34,067
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:36,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,400
<i> We couldn't stop Mr. Chan.</i>

24
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:47,333
<i>But there's one more way.
It's time to visit our son.</i>

25
00:01:47,333 --> 00:01:48,900
<i> They hit me! The agent!</i>

26
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,667
<i> They forced me to confess!</i>

27
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:54,400
<i>I'll make sure to shut you
up before you drop my name.</i>

28
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:57,867
<i>The admin put you on
preventive suspension.</i>

29
00:01:57,867 --> 00:02:02,067
<i>Leave your badge
and gun behind before leaving.</i>

30
00:02:02,067 --> 00:02:04,867
<i>Just follow everything
I ordered you to do.</i>

31
00:02:04,867 --> 00:02:06,700
<i> I want a clean job.</i>

32
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:07,933
<i> Get out! Hurry!</i>

33
00:02:07,933 --> 00:02:09,333
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [GRUNTS IN PAIN]

34
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:11,867
<i>Hey!
[ENGINE REVVING]</i>

35
00:02:11,867 --> 00:02:14,633
[PUNCHES AND KICKS LANDING]

36
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,333
- What's your name, by the way?
<i> - Gabo.</i>

37
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:18,100
<i>Looks like your bike got
busted because of me.</i>

38
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:19,200
<i> Here's money to help fix it.</i>

39
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,900
<i>This isn't enough,
you saved my life.</i>

40
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,533
Someday, I'll help you out, too.

41
00:02:23,533 --> 00:02:24,833
<i> Thank you so much.</i>

42
00:02:27,967 --> 00:02:29,933
What happened to that big mouth?

43
00:02:29,933 --> 00:02:32,000
You were so tough earlier.
[KICK LANDS]

44
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,500
You've got some nerve.

45
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,733
[PUNCHES AND KICKS LANDING]

46
00:02:36,967 --> 00:02:40,400
As for you, you need more
blood on your face.

47
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:43,167
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [GRUNTS IN PAIN]

48
00:02:43,167 --> 00:02:45,733
And you, you're so arrogant,
huh?

49
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:48,900
[PUNCHES AND KICKS LANDING]

50
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:52,167
[YELLING]
Argh! Ah! Ah!

51
00:02:52,167 --> 00:02:54,667
What?! So tough, huh?

52
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:58,567
If you want to sue,
I have a video!

53
00:02:58,567 --> 00:02:59,900
Really?

54
00:03:01,833 --> 00:03:03,033
Awesome.

55
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:10,833
- Nice!
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

56
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:13,800
Hey! Don't mess
with my food over there!

57
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,533
- Told you guys.
- Hey, you don't listen.

58
00:03:15,533 --> 00:03:16,633
Don't mess with it.

59
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,433
- It's this guy's fault.
- Told you guys.

60
00:03:18,433 --> 00:03:21,400
Hey, you three, come here.

61
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:22,800
- Us, sir?
- Get over here.

62
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,733
He's calling, go over there.

63
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:26,867
Do you need something,
Mister Rudy?

64
00:03:26,867 --> 00:03:27,967
Sir?

65
00:03:27,967 --> 00:03:30,567
Aren't you guys
Django's friends?

66
00:03:30,567 --> 00:03:31,767
Why are you here?

67
00:03:31,767 --> 00:03:33,600
Mr. Rudy, it's really
a long story.

68
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:36,600
If we tell you, you'll tire out
and end up back in the hospital.

69
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:37,900
Yes.

70
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:41,367
All you need to know, Mister
Rudy, is these three fools

71
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:44,633
helped Gabo a lot
to get you out of the hospital.

72
00:03:44,633 --> 00:03:45,733
Yes, Mister Rudy.

73
00:03:45,733 --> 00:03:49,267
He needs us for his work.
And we're there for him.

74
00:03:49,267 --> 00:03:52,900
Hey, you guys! I know
what kind of people you are.

75
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,867
Don't lead Gabo down
a bad path.

76
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:57,267
- Be more like Gabo.
- Yes, Mister Rudy.

77
00:03:57,267 --> 00:03:58,733
Gabo is a good influence,

78
00:03:58,733 --> 00:04:01,433
that's why we follow his lead,
right?

79
00:04:01,433 --> 00:04:03,267
- Yeah.
- Right!

80
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,233
Cheers!

81
00:04:06,233 --> 00:04:07,733
- Boss.
- Go ahead, boss.

82
00:04:07,733 --> 00:04:09,800
I'm sure they can pull off
the mission.

83
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:13,733
How did your mission go?
Was it a success?

84
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:17,800
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,800
What?

86
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,067
You passed it to someone else?

87
00:04:24,067 --> 00:04:25,767
I let the newbies
take charge, Pa,

88
00:04:25,767 --> 00:04:27,733
so they can show
what they've got

89
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:29,867
and learn along the way.

90
00:04:29,867 --> 00:04:31,533
Don't worry, Pa.

91
00:04:31,533 --> 00:04:34,167
I gave them clear instructions
on what to do.

92
00:04:35,167 --> 00:04:36,633
You expect me not to worry?

93
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:41,200
Didn't we agree you'd be
the one to do it yourself?

94
00:04:41,633 --> 00:04:43,300
Why did you let
others handle it?

95
00:04:44,133 --> 00:04:45,433
What if they mess it up?

96
00:04:45,833 --> 00:04:48,600
The job's far too simple
to go wrong.

97
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,333
Even Pulgas himself could do it.

98
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,800
[LAUGHING]

99
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,600
[PAQUITO]
This is the problem with you.

100
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:59,100
You're showing complete
disregard for my orders.

101
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,467
Hang on, Pa.

102
00:05:01,833 --> 00:05:04,300
I thought I was going to be
the next king here.

103
00:05:04,633 --> 00:05:07,000
So why are you questioning
my decisions?

104
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,100
You're making me look
like I'm under you.

105
00:05:09,433 --> 00:05:12,067
You'd better know your place!

106
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,600
If you think you are
the king here...

107
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,900
Remember this.

108
00:05:17,267 --> 00:05:19,967
I'm the one
who built your kingdom!

109
00:05:20,267 --> 00:05:23,333
If you believe you're the one
to be obeyed here,

110
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:24,933
then you're mistaken.

111
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:27,100
Because the truth is,

112
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:31,333
the people's loyalty
still belongs to me!

113
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:38,267
[BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

114
00:05:47,233 --> 00:05:48,700
- [MUSIC ENDS]
- [ENGINE RUMBLING]

115
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,767
- Good morning.
- Sir.

116
00:05:52,767 --> 00:05:53,767
Sir.

117
00:05:53,767 --> 00:05:55,767
- Sir.
- Well, any update?

118
00:05:55,767 --> 00:05:58,033
Sir, there's still no word
from Django.

119
00:05:58,467 --> 00:06:00,800
But this morning,
Salvador's fate is sealed.

120
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:05,033
The group has already been
informed about his residence

121
00:06:05,033 --> 00:06:06,400
and likely route.

122
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:11,600
[UMALI] Our men have been told
to stage it as a robbery,

123
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:15,300
so no one suspects the truth.

124
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:19,200
Today, the reporter becomes
the story.

125
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:23,467
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:24,467
Salvador?

127
00:06:25,567 --> 00:06:26,700
[ESTRELLA]
What happened to you?

128
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:28,600
I'm going to file
a police report.

129
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:30,067
Where do I go for thatl?

130
00:06:30,067 --> 00:06:31,700
Arandia, accompany him.

131
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:32,733
Yes, sir.

132
00:06:32,733 --> 00:06:34,200
Sir, this way. Follow me.

133
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,800
[ARANDIA] Right this way, sir.

134
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:45,267
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,600
If it happens...

136
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,767
- That's true.
- He'll be gone forever.

137
00:06:48,767 --> 00:06:50,567
[SANTOS WHISPERS]
Sir, sir. It's Salvador.

138
00:06:58,333 --> 00:07:05,333
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

139
00:07:06,167 --> 00:07:07,333
What is this?

140
00:07:07,767 --> 00:07:09,267
And here I thought--

141
00:07:10,333 --> 00:07:13,100
Damn it.
He got terribly lucky.

142
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:16,067
[INHALES SHARPLY]

143
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:24,100
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

144
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:26,133
[WOMAN]
Gabo, your father is home!

145
00:07:26,133 --> 00:07:27,533
[INDISTINCT CHATTER, LAUGHTER]

146
00:07:27,533 --> 00:07:30,367
Mister Elton, Gabo is back
with the motorcycle!

147
00:07:30,367 --> 00:07:35,767
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:07:35,767 --> 00:07:37,200
What happened
to the motorcycle?!

149
00:07:37,733 --> 00:07:39,800
[RUDY] What's that noise?
Go and check it out.

150
00:07:40,467 --> 00:07:42,667
What did you do to it?!

151
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,233
- [DANTE] Gabo's finally back.
- Come on.

152
00:07:46,233 --> 00:07:47,767
Why is it covered in mud?!

153
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,200
- [BETCHAY] Careful now.
- The fender's broken too!

154
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,533
Hey, be careful!

155
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:52,300
Come on, Gabo!

156
00:07:52,767 --> 00:07:53,900
You might lose your footing.

157
00:07:54,267 --> 00:07:56,067
[ELTON]
You never do anything right!

158
00:07:56,067 --> 00:07:58,100
[CROWD MURMURING]

159
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:00,033
- Oh no...
- This is bad.

160
00:08:00,033 --> 00:08:03,067
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

161
00:08:03,067 --> 00:08:05,667
[RUDY] Gabo, what happened?

162
00:08:05,667 --> 00:08:08,067
[BETCHAY]
What did you do this time?!

163
00:08:08,067 --> 00:08:09,767
My goodness!

164
00:08:09,767 --> 00:08:10,900
[ELTON] Rudy!

165
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:13,033
Look at what your son did
to the motorcycle.

166
00:08:13,033 --> 00:08:15,067
The owner will pick it up today!

167
00:08:15,867 --> 00:08:17,300
[BETCHAY] For heaven's sake!

168
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:20,433
Rudy, look at what your son
did this time!

169
00:08:20,433 --> 00:08:23,000
Please, Betchay!
Let's stay out of it!

170
00:08:23,033 --> 00:08:25,467
- But we're already involved!
- [DANTE] Gabo, what did you do?

171
00:08:25,467 --> 00:08:26,867
You just brought problems!

172
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:27,967
[RUDY] That's enough!

173
00:08:27,967 --> 00:08:30,233
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:08:30,233 --> 00:08:31,267
Gabo...

175
00:08:31,967 --> 00:08:33,533
What exactly happened?

176
00:08:36,033 --> 00:08:38,933
Pa, I had an accident.

177
00:08:38,933 --> 00:08:45,900
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

178
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,033
Mister Rudy!

179
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,700
- Oh no.
- So you're finally discharged!

180
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,033
Cover it up! Hide it!

181
00:08:59,033 --> 00:09:01,067
- Don't let him see it!
- I'm back for my motorcycle!

182
00:09:01,067 --> 00:09:02,367
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:09:02,367 --> 00:09:03,367
[RUDY] Uh...

184
00:09:03,933 --> 00:09:06,200
Well, got the payment ready?

185
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,400
I've got it. How much is it?

186
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:09,867
- [RUDY] Uh...
- [OVERLAPPING MURMURS]

187
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:14,567
Can you give me
a few more days?

188
00:09:14,567 --> 00:09:17,067
The engine's still rough.
I need to fine-tune it.

189
00:09:17,067 --> 00:09:19,667
You had it for a long time!
You're delaying the pickup day!

190
00:09:19,667 --> 00:09:21,067
Is this a scam?

191
00:09:21,067 --> 00:09:24,900
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

192
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:25,967
[THROUGH GRITTED TEETH] Rudy.

193
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:28,333
Just tell him the truth

194
00:09:28,367 --> 00:09:30,700
so that we don't get
into trouble.

195
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:32,500
Why? What happened?

196
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:34,233
Uh, you see...
[CLEARS THROAT]

197
00:09:34,233 --> 00:09:35,633
We have a minor issue.

198
00:09:35,633 --> 00:09:37,400
It just had a little scratch.

199
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,333
But it's nothing that
I can't fix.

200
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:41,467
- A scratch?
- Yes, a tiny one.

201
00:09:43,533 --> 00:09:45,133
- Step aside!
- [SCREAMING]

202
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:48,333
A scratch?!
Are you blind?

203
00:09:48,333 --> 00:09:49,400
It looks ruined!

204
00:09:50,133 --> 00:09:52,167
- Look at it!
- Sir...

205
00:09:52,167 --> 00:09:54,400
Keep your cool.
Don't get upset so easily.

206
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,900
Get away from me,
or I'll smack you!

207
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:57,233
- Sorry, sorry!
- Hey, hey, hey!

208
00:09:57,533 --> 00:09:59,900
[RUDY] Brando, can you give
me a little more time?

209
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:03,467
Trust me, when you pick this up,
it'll look as good as brand new.

210
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:05,267
[BRANDO]
I'm boarding the ship tomorrow!

211
00:10:05,567 --> 00:10:09,333
The next time I come back,
I should be getting it.

212
00:10:09,333 --> 00:10:11,667
Or else we'll see each other
in court!

213
00:10:11,667 --> 00:10:13,433
- [BETCHAY] Oh my! No!
- [MAMENG] Good grief!

214
00:10:13,433 --> 00:10:14,667
Sir! Sir!

215
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:17,600
Sir, please, let's not go there.

216
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:20,533
You heard Rudy.
He can fix it.

217
00:10:20,533 --> 00:10:21,833
Sir, please.

218
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:23,267
You're all the same!

219
00:10:23,267 --> 00:10:25,167
A bunch of swindlers! Liars!

220
00:10:29,067 --> 00:10:32,067
[BETCHAY] Did you see what
your son has done now?

221
00:10:32,067 --> 00:10:33,233
Another mess!

222
00:10:33,233 --> 00:10:34,300
[RUDY] That's enough!

223
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,933
I just got out of the hospital.

224
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:39,467
You know, we should
probably talk at home.

225
00:10:39,467 --> 00:10:42,367
[BETCHAY] Come on, come on.
Let's go inside. Be careful.

226
00:10:44,267 --> 00:10:45,467
[RUDY] Let's go.

227
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:47,000
- [MAMENG] A lawsuit, Rudy.
- [BETCHAY] What will we do?

228
00:10:50,433 --> 00:10:51,467
[MAMENG] Hah...

229
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:54,800
[BETCHAY] Slowly, slowly.

230
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:56,900
- You should sit.
- Sit here.

231
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:00,600
Gabo, you've only been gone
for a while.

232
00:11:01,333 --> 00:11:02,800
What happened?

233
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,300
[TOLITS] Gabo, what happened
to the motorcycle?

234
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,400
Wasn't it okay?

235
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:08,633
It was still in good condition
when we got it back.

236
00:11:11,167 --> 00:11:17,433
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:11:17,433 --> 00:11:18,567
Pa.

238
00:11:20,433 --> 00:11:24,233
When we separated ways,
when I was on my way home...

239
00:11:25,867 --> 00:11:28,333
I saw a man getting mugged.

240
00:11:28,867 --> 00:11:30,233
They almost killed him.

241
00:11:30,933 --> 00:11:32,333
So I saved him.

242
00:11:33,033 --> 00:11:36,033
I didn't mean to crash
the motorcycle.

243
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:44,033
[MAN] Boss Django, they're here.

244
00:11:44,967 --> 00:11:50,933
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

245
00:11:50,933 --> 00:11:52,067
What happened?

246
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,000
Why do you look
like that?

247
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:02,500
What, one small reporter
beat you all up?

248
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:05,133
No, boss. We did what you said.

249
00:12:05,133 --> 00:12:07,000
It's not the reporter
who beat us up.

250
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,033
Someone came and intervened.

251
00:12:09,033 --> 00:12:12,000
- Who?
- We don't know, boss.

252
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,567
But he even threatened us.

253
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:15,300
How many were they?

254
00:12:16,333 --> 00:12:18,700
Boss, it was just one person.

255
00:12:20,733 --> 00:12:24,533
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:12:24,533 --> 00:12:26,167
[DJANGO CHUCKLING]

257
00:12:26,167 --> 00:12:27,233
One person?

258
00:12:27,233 --> 00:12:28,900
Only one person did that?!

259
00:12:29,533 --> 00:12:30,833
Stupid!

260
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:35,467
[BLOWS LANDING]

261
00:12:35,467 --> 00:12:38,433
- Boss! Boss, boss, boss, boss!
- You idiots!

262
00:12:38,433 --> 00:12:39,600
[PAQUITO] Django!

263
00:12:40,533 --> 00:12:41,700
This is all your fault!

264
00:12:42,433 --> 00:12:45,433
If you've just followed
what I told you,

265
00:12:45,433 --> 00:12:47,333
they wouldn't have failed!

266
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:50,467
But they did follow my order.
They mugged him!

267
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:51,533
But did they beat him up?

268
00:12:51,533 --> 00:12:53,800
They're the ones
who got beaten up!

269
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:57,600
That wouldn't have happened
if you had been there!

270
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,900
They said someone intervened!

271
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:02,133
I'll look for that bastard!
I'll make him pay!

272
00:13:02,133 --> 00:13:04,800
It's over! You're too late!

273
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:08,433
If you had just been there,
this wouldn't have happened!

274
00:13:08,433 --> 00:13:11,933
Next time,
do what I tell you to do!

275
00:13:11,933 --> 00:13:13,800
Don't make others do your job!

276
00:13:15,433 --> 00:13:22,433
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

277
00:13:31,633 --> 00:13:38,533
[BLOWS, KICKS LANDING]

278
00:13:39,633 --> 00:13:45,433
[BLOWS, KICKS LANDING]

279
00:13:45,433 --> 00:13:47,200
[BODY THUDS]

280
00:13:48,433 --> 00:13:49,633
You're all useless!

281
00:13:50,367 --> 00:13:53,367
You're all incompetent!

282
00:13:53,367 --> 00:13:54,533
- [KICK LANDS]
- [MAN GROANS]

283
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:56,733
- [MAN 1] Boss!
- [MAN 2] Don't, boss.

284
00:13:56,733 --> 00:13:57,733
[KICK LANDS]

285
00:13:57,733 --> 00:13:58,900
- [GUNSHOTS]
- Boss, don't-- Argh!

286
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:01,400
[GUNSHOTS]

287
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,167
- Leave! Leave!
- [GUNSHOTS]

288
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,600
- Leave! You rats!
- [GUNSHOTS]

289
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:11,233
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:14:14,133 --> 00:14:15,467
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

291
00:14:15,467 --> 00:14:18,433
Here, drink some water.

292
00:14:20,967 --> 00:14:22,367
[WATER TRICKLING]

293
00:14:22,367 --> 00:14:23,833
- Hmm.
- [PITCHER THUDS]

294
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:27,400
Django is getting cocky.

295
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,200
He's arrogant.

296
00:14:31,033 --> 00:14:32,800
He doesn't listen to me anymore.

297
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,900
Who else would he take after?

298
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:36,500
You, of coure.

299
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,433
- What?
- He's just like you.

300
00:14:39,033 --> 00:14:41,367
You think so highly of yourself.

301
00:14:41,367 --> 00:14:43,567
You don't listen
to anyone either.

302
00:14:43,567 --> 00:14:46,933
Because you believe
your word is the law.

303
00:14:46,933 --> 00:14:51,067
It's because I've led
our group for many years.

304
00:14:51,067 --> 00:14:52,200
I believe

305
00:14:52,833 --> 00:14:56,200
I'm doing a great job,
that's why everything's well.

306
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,633
The problem is

307
00:14:57,633 --> 00:15:01,600
Django is putting his ego first.

308
00:15:01,633 --> 00:15:05,067
You didn't fall short
in guiding Django.

309
00:15:05,067 --> 00:15:09,233
And you shaped him
to be just like you.

310
00:15:09,233 --> 00:15:13,133
I wouldn't be surprised
if he becomes better than you.

311
00:15:14,667 --> 00:15:17,167
I'll get going.
We have a lot of work to do.

312
00:15:17,167 --> 00:15:22,300
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

313
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,267
[MUSIC FADES]

314
00:15:23,267 --> 00:15:24,700
Hmm. [TONGUE CLICKS]

315
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:26,167
Gabo. [CLEARS THROAT]

316
00:15:28,367 --> 00:15:30,667
Tell us the truth.
What exactly happened?

317
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:37,667
Auntie Betchay,
I'm telling you the truth.

318
00:15:37,667 --> 00:15:40,467
I saved someone, that's why
the motorcycle got ruined.

319
00:15:41,433 --> 00:15:42,733
Oh, please.

320
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:45,633
When are you going
to stop doubting Gabo?

321
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:49,267
Rudy already said
he's turning over a new leaf.

322
00:15:49,267 --> 00:15:52,300
How would he do that
if you keep judging him?

323
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:54,600
I'm just making sure.

324
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:57,100
Because I don't believe
that's what happened.

325
00:16:04,367 --> 00:16:07,900
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:12,800
Pa, the man I saved
gave me money.

327
00:16:13,767 --> 00:16:16,000
Here. It's for--

328
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,133
- Hey!
- Ah!

329
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:20,133
That's Gabo's. Give it back.

330
00:16:20,133 --> 00:16:21,133
Why?

331
00:16:30,267 --> 00:16:31,700
He just gave it to us.

332
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:32,733
[RUDY] Give it back.

333
00:16:33,633 --> 00:16:34,967
Son, take it.

334
00:16:38,667 --> 00:16:40,067
[RUDY] That's your money.

335
00:16:40,067 --> 00:16:42,233
- Come on.
- No, Pa, it's for you.

336
00:16:42,267 --> 00:16:44,000
Hear that? It's for us.

337
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,067
No. Come on, son.
Take it. It's yours.

338
00:16:47,333 --> 00:16:48,433
Let it go.

339
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:52,833
Let it go.

340
00:16:56,800 --> 00:17:03,833
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

341
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:13,000
[BETCHAY GRUNTS] Argh!

342
00:17:19,633 --> 00:17:20,867
What are you doing?!

343
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:26,567
- Argh! Let it go!
- It's mine! I'll give it back!

344
00:17:26,567 --> 00:17:28,900
Let go of me! I'm doing it!

345
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:30,067
Argh!

346
00:17:30,067 --> 00:17:33,367
I did it! Why do we have to?
That should've been ours!

347
00:17:33,367 --> 00:17:36,567
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

348
00:17:36,567 --> 00:17:38,633
Gabo, that's a lot of cash.

349
00:17:38,633 --> 00:17:40,933
Maybe you can treat us to lunch.

350
00:17:40,933 --> 00:17:43,033
We also worked hard
to get the motorcycle back.

351
00:17:43,033 --> 00:17:44,967
- Yeah!
- We even got bitten by a dog.

352
00:17:44,967 --> 00:17:46,300
Good thing
we were wearing pants.

353
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:47,567
- Yeah.
- That's true, Gabo.

354
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:49,267
Lunch on you wouldn't be so bad.

355
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:50,967
We risk our lives
for the motorcycle.

356
00:17:50,967 --> 00:17:52,800
He's right Gabo.

357
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:54,867
Treat your friends.

358
00:17:54,867 --> 00:17:57,067
They helped you big time.

359
00:17:58,567 --> 00:17:59,500
Okay.

360
00:18:00,067 --> 00:18:01,033
I'll get dressed.

361
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:03,900
Gabo!

362
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,833
What about the cost
of the repair?

363
00:18:06,833 --> 00:18:09,867
Elton, I'll take care of that.
I'll find a way.

364
00:18:11,433 --> 00:18:12,667
Go on, son.

365
00:18:14,233 --> 00:18:17,933
Gabo, maybe you can lend me
any spare dough?

366
00:18:17,933 --> 00:18:19,233
Hey, hey. hey.

367
00:18:20,133 --> 00:18:21,533
Stop it, Dante.

368
00:18:21,567 --> 00:18:23,067
- Stop it.
- Oh, come on.

369
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:26,933
[BETCHAY CLEARS THROAT]

370
00:18:26,933 --> 00:18:30,633
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

371
00:18:30,633 --> 00:18:31,700
Sir?

372
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Yes?

373
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:40,033
Sir, with everything
that has happened,

374
00:18:40,033 --> 00:18:42,500
I'm accepting my suspension
because I deserve it.

375
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,833
I just have a few suggestions
for the people we've arrested.

376
00:18:46,833 --> 00:18:47,800
Let me hear it.

377
00:18:48,633 --> 00:18:50,167
At least now

378
00:18:50,167 --> 00:18:53,467
you can tell me
what you're thinking

379
00:18:53,467 --> 00:18:55,367
before you just act on it.

380
00:18:56,433 --> 00:18:57,800
Have a seat.

381
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:02,367
Sir, I'm just thinking,

382
00:19:02,367 --> 00:19:04,267
why don't we put Mr. Chan

383
00:19:04,267 --> 00:19:06,233
and Tiger together
in the same cell?

384
00:19:06,233 --> 00:19:09,200
Right now,
Mr. Chan doesn't talk at all.

385
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:12,867
Their clashing
could reveal the truth.

386
00:19:12,867 --> 00:19:14,300
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:15,833
They're going to be like...

388
00:19:16,933 --> 00:19:19,233
aggressive spiders
trapped in a box.

389
00:19:21,233 --> 00:19:22,333
Yes, sir.

390
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:24,233
That's a good plan, Sam.

391
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,100
A good one.

392
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:28,500
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

393
00:19:32,567 --> 00:19:33,567
Sam?

394
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,833
What happened?

395
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,467
I'm suspended.

396
00:19:41,467 --> 00:19:42,467
- Huh?
- [ROBERT HUFFS]

397
00:19:42,467 --> 00:19:43,367
Ma'am...

398
00:19:44,167 --> 00:19:45,433
For how long?

399
00:19:46,267 --> 00:19:47,633
Indefinitely.

400
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,367
That can still be lifted, Sam.

401
00:19:51,367 --> 00:19:53,100
Want me to talk to the admin?

402
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:56,633
I'll get through to Delgado.
I'll explain everything.

403
00:19:56,833 --> 00:19:57,967
I'll do it for you.

404
00:19:57,967 --> 00:19:59,233
You don't have to.

405
00:20:00,767 --> 00:20:02,167
Team, listen.

406
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:04,700
I'll leave our cases to you.

407
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:08,033
Don't worry, Ma'am Sam.
We'll continue what you started.

408
00:20:08,033 --> 00:20:10,367
Yes, ma'am.
And we'll keep you up to date.

409
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:14,000
As your team leader,

410
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:17,500
I hope you learn
from my mistake.

411
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:20,200
Don't let your emotions
get the best of you.

412
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,600
Don't be like me.

413
00:20:22,333 --> 00:20:24,433
Sorry for dragging you all
into my mess.

414
00:20:24,433 --> 00:20:26,367
Honestly, it's nothing.

415
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,933
It happens to the best of us.

416
00:20:28,933 --> 00:20:30,700
No, it shouldn't.

417
00:20:31,333 --> 00:20:33,000
What I did was wrong.

418
00:20:34,467 --> 00:20:36,033
I deserve that suspension.

419
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:39,800
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

420
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:42,333
Go on, guys.
I still have to clear my table.

421
00:20:45,267 --> 00:20:46,267
[SAM CLEARS THROAT]

422
00:20:48,467 --> 00:20:49,700
- Come on!
- Let's go!

423
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:51,600
- Let's get going!
- Off we go!

424
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,767
[BETCHAY] Gabo! Psst!

425
00:20:52,767 --> 00:20:55,600
- Ow! Miss Betchay!
- Gabo, wait! Give me a minute.

426
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:59,400
You know your father is just
too shy to take the money.

427
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:01,500
He's too prideful, you see.

428
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:04,900
But I know you know how costly
our expenses are at home.

429
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:06,767
Not to mention, he needs
his maintenance meds.

430
00:21:06,767 --> 00:21:08,767
Why don't you give half of it?

431
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,500
[RUDY] Hey, Betchay!

432
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:12,400
Can you quit it?

433
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:15,500
[BETCHAY] You'll just let them
waste 10,000 pesos?

434
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:18,633
[RUDY] It's not a waste
if they're going to have fun!

435
00:21:18,633 --> 00:21:20,100
Go on, Gabo.
Be on your way.

436
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:21,233
Take care, okay?

437
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,800
- Yes, Pa.
- Bye, Miss Betchay!

438
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:26,733
- We'll eat our hearts out.
- Yeah, yeah!

439
00:21:26,733 --> 00:21:28,733
[MOCKING VOICE]
"Yeah, yeah!"

440
00:21:28,733 --> 00:21:31,000
- [TEKLA CACKLING]
- Why don't they come along?

441
00:21:32,733 --> 00:21:33,667
[BETCHAY SIGHS]

442
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:34,633
- Sir.
- Hm?

443
00:21:34,633 --> 00:21:36,000
[WHISPERING]
This is your chance now.

444
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,133
What chance?

445
00:21:39,133 --> 00:21:42,567
Sir, Ma'am Sam is sad.
She's vulnerable right now.

446
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:44,533
She needs a shoulder
to cry on.

447
00:21:45,767 --> 00:21:48,100
- [CHORTLES]
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

448
00:21:48,100 --> 00:21:49,967
You're good.
You're really good!

449
00:21:49,967 --> 00:21:52,500
Of course, I'm the best.
Because you're the best!

450
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:53,667
You got this, sir.

451
00:21:53,667 --> 00:21:56,333
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

452
00:21:56,333 --> 00:21:58,100
[CLEARS THROAT] Guys!

453
00:21:58,933 --> 00:22:02,667
I know this is not
a good day for Sam,

454
00:22:02,667 --> 00:22:05,067
so I was just thinking...

455
00:22:05,067 --> 00:22:08,900
Since we are a team
and we are here for Sam,

456
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:12,600
why don't we hang out
and go for some drinks?

457
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,667
First round's on me.

458
00:22:13,667 --> 00:22:15,267
Just the first round, sir?

459
00:22:16,300 --> 00:22:18,933
For Sam, the sky's the limit!

460
00:22:18,933 --> 00:22:20,500
- Alright!
- Yes!

461
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:22,300
- We're all game!
- You heard them.

462
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:23,667
They're all game.

463
00:22:23,667 --> 00:22:24,833
What do you say, Sam?

464
00:22:24,833 --> 00:22:27,100
Sam, you're suspended.

465
00:22:27,100 --> 00:22:29,033
I don't know when
I will see you again.

466
00:22:29,033 --> 00:22:30,933
Honestly, I'll miss you.

467
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:35,033
And look at me. I'm in pain.
I got shot, remember?

468
00:22:35,033 --> 00:22:37,033
Let me have this, please?

469
00:22:37,033 --> 00:22:38,200
[SEBASTIAN] Mm-hmm!

470
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:42,167
Come on, Ma'am Sam.
She needs her pain reliever!

471
00:22:43,733 --> 00:22:46,333
Ma'am Sam,
let Sir Seb do this for you.

472
00:22:46,333 --> 00:22:49,933
Yeah, ma'am. Let's go.
Besides, it's his treat.

473
00:22:49,967 --> 00:22:53,167
It's a perfect way to unwind
after everything that happened.

474
00:22:53,167 --> 00:22:54,667
Well? Is it a yes?

475
00:22:54,667 --> 00:22:56,400
- Yes?
- Yes?

476
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:58,833
- Will you say yes?
- She's going to say yes.

477
00:22:58,833 --> 00:23:00,467
Yes? Yes? Yes?

478
00:23:00,467 --> 00:23:02,167
- Yes? Yes?
- Yes?

479
00:23:02,167 --> 00:23:04,600
- Yes? It's a yes!
- [CHEERING]

480
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:06,433
- Whoo-hoo!
- Alright, guys!

481
00:23:06,433 --> 00:23:09,600
The sky is the limit!
Anywhere and anything you like.

482
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:12,067
- For Sam. Alright! Let's go!
- Where should we go?

483
00:23:12,067 --> 00:23:13,900
- Where's a good place?
- Come on.

484
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:15,467
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

485
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:19,933
Where do you want to go?
Any suggestions?

486
00:23:19,933 --> 00:23:22,467
[KAREN] Remember that place
we wanted to check out?

487
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:24,333
Ow, I accidentally moved my arm.

488
00:23:24,333 --> 00:23:26,300
[RALLOS] There's a new bar
that just opened.

489
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:27,400
[SEBASTIAN] Where is it?

490
00:23:27,933 --> 00:23:29,533
[BINOY] Gabo, where are you
taking us?

491
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:31,400
[TOLITS] I'm sure it's going
to be a great spot!

492
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:38,433
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

493
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:44,567
<i>I'm still haunted
by the past, Papa.</i>

494
00:23:44,567 --> 00:23:46,900
<i>Spare my family!
Just kill me!</i>

495
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:49,000
<i>- Mama!
- [GASPS]</i>

496
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:51,900
<i>I need to find out
who killed Mama.</i>

497
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:54,167
<i>Mariano. It's no surprise
that you're Victor's father.</i>

498
00:23:54,167 --> 00:23:55,900
<i>The apple doesn't fall far
from the tree.</i>

499
00:23:55,933 --> 00:23:57,467
<i> Whatever you're planning,</i>

500
00:23:57,467 --> 00:23:59,600
<i>I'll make sure
you won't succeed.</i>

501
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:01,733
<i> Whoever gets in the way,
eliminate them.</i>

502
00:24:01,733 --> 00:24:05,200
<i>I want to know who killed her.
Do you know who did it?!</i>

503
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:07,133
<i> You didn't just bring shame
to our family.</i>

504
00:24:07,133 --> 00:24:09,133
<i>You also brought us
so much pain!</i>

505
00:24:09,133 --> 00:24:12,033
<i>All of us are devastated
by my brother's death!</i>

506
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:16,700
<i>And I keep praying every day
to earn your forgiveness!</i>

507
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:19,500
<i> - RJ!
</i>- [GUNSHOT]

508
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:22,133
<i>At last! I can finally taste
some proper food!</i>

509
00:24:22,133 --> 00:24:24,533
<i> I'll make sure you all
drown in booze!</i>

510
00:24:24,533 --> 00:24:25,700
<i>- Alright!
- Yeah!</i>

511
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:26,833
[LAUGHTER]

512
00:24:27,367 --> 00:24:30,233
<i>Why are you staring?
Do you have the hots for me?</i>

513
00:24:31,100 --> 00:24:37,867
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

514
00:24:54,567 --> 00:24:56,533
<i> It's a pleasant surprise</i>

515
00:24:56,533 --> 00:24:58,867
<i>that there are still
good people like him.</i>

516
00:24:58,867 --> 00:25:00,800
<i> His name is Gabo.</i>

517
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:02,600
<i> That runt got even bolder.</i>

518
00:25:02,633 --> 00:25:04,333
<i> You're cops, aren't you?
You can handle him.</i>

519
00:25:04,333 --> 00:25:06,100
You think you're all that, huh?

520
00:25:06,100 --> 00:25:08,367
<i>Pull the trigger!
Let's see you try!</i>

521
00:25:08,367 --> 00:25:10,567
<i>You're going to work
for Gabo's enemy?!</i>

522
00:25:10,567 --> 00:25:12,533
<i>You want me to worry
about my body?</i>

523
00:25:12,533 --> 00:25:14,767
<i>We don't even have
enough to eat!</i>

524
00:25:14,767 --> 00:25:16,767
What good is my pride, anyway?!

525
00:25:16,767 --> 00:25:19,500
<i> I'm so sick of being poor!</i>

526
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:21,733
[OVERLAPPING SCREAMS]

527
00:25:21,733 --> 00:25:24,033
- Keep tabs on Samantha Jacinto.
- [GUNSHOTS]

528
00:25:24,033 --> 00:25:26,267
<i>We must get rid of her
as soon as possible.</i>

529
00:25:26,267 --> 00:25:28,300
<i>Well, Samantha?!
You still alive?!</i>

530
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:29,367
[GUNSHOTS]

531
00:25:29,367 --> 00:25:32,267
<i>We're talking about
my agent's life here!</i>

532
00:25:32,267 --> 00:25:35,367
<i>If your agent dies, don't pin
the blame on someone else!</i>

533
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:37,367
<i> Go ahead! Pull the trigger!</i>

534
00:25:37,367 --> 00:25:38,400
[GUNSHOTS]

535
00:25:40,167 --> 00:25:42,800
[GUNSHOTS]

536
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:44,033
<i> Django!</i>

537
00:25:44,033 --> 00:25:45,667
<i> Let blood be spilled
here in Tondo</i>

538
00:25:45,667 --> 00:25:47,567
<i> until only one group prevails!</i>

539
00:25:47,567 --> 00:25:50,667
- [MEN GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]
